<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{title}} · {{model.lesson}}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{description}}">
  {{!-- `root` is the climb back to the build root, set by each page in its
        {{#extend}} hash. Relative, so the page works inside a package: an LMS
        serves the package's files from wherever it unpacks them. --}}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{root}}{{asset 'css/course.css'}}">
  {{!-- The SCORM 1.2 bridge, in <head> so it runs before anything the page
        embeds. In an LMS it starts the session; with `complete` unset the
        page's own script says when it is done, and `complete="seen"` makes a
        page complete when it is seen. Only a page that keeps no place should
        use `seen`: in Moodle, a completed page reopens in review mode and
        saves nothing more. On the web, or in an IMS content package, it finds
        no LMS and does nothing. --}}
  {{scormBridge complete=complete}}
</head>
<body>
  <main class="lesson">
    <p class="lesson__eyebrow">{{config.site.name}} · {{model.lesson}}</p>
    {{#block "body"}}{{/block}}
  </main>
</body>
</html>
